  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Binay Prakash vs The State Of Jharkhand on 18 November, 2016",
    "facts": "It has also been submitted that two persons of the Department had taken the sample and in the case in which Burfi was taken for testing one of them Gulab Lakra, Food, Safety Officer, Ranchi became complainant. It has also been submitted that on the same day at the same hotel premises of the petitioner, the food article namely Paneer was also seized by the Food Safety Officer and proceeding was initiated before the Deputy Commissioner, Ranchi which vide order dated 13.08.2014 the same was dropped, as the samples were not sealed in presence of independent witnesses as per provisions of Food Safety Standard Act, 2006. It has also been submitted that the complainant of C-III Case No. 254 of 2013, which has been lodged with respect to Burfi, was the witness in Food Safety & Standards Case No. 43 of 2013-14 initiated with respect to Paneer. Learned counsel further submits that contradictory reports submitted by two different labs i.e. by the State Food Analyst and the Referral Lab, Mysore, suggests that the department has not been able to establish case against the petitioner beyond doubt.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Arun Kumar Pandey, learned APP prays for and is allowed four weeks' time to seek instruction and file counter affidavit.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "Mr. Arun Kumar Pandey, learned APP prays for and is allowed four weeks' time to seek instruction and file counter affidavit.",
